 *   **Overestimation:** The expanded triangle covers more area than the original, leading to unnecessary fragment shader invocations for discarded pixels [S1, unofficial].
 
 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** $O(1)$ per triangle in the geometry shader (constant number of operations). $O(N)$ in the fragment shader, where $N$ is the number of pixels covered by the expanded triangle [G].
-*   **Memory Complexity:** Minimal additional memory in the geometry shader. Fragment shader state is per-fragment [G].
